              "racialFeaturesMarkdown": "- Height Range:\n  - Male: 5'10\" - 6'5\" (155cm to 198cm)\n  - Female: 5'6\" - 6'1\" (170cm to 185cm)\n\n- Weight Range:\n  - 55 kg to 90 kg \n\n- Skin:\n  - Smooth skin with an almost translucent appearance\n  - Often cool and slightly damp to the touch\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Pale Blue\n    - Seafoam Grey\n    - Silver White\n    - Mist Grey\n    - Deep Ocean Blue\n\n- Hair:\n  - Constantly appears wet regardless of environment\n  - Moves subtly as if suspended underwater\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Black\n    - Dark Blue\n    - Silver\n    - White\n    - Sea Green\n\n- Eyes:\n  - Deep reflective eyes that resemble still water\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Silver\n    - Pale Blue\n    - White\n    - Sea Green\n    - Moonlit Grey\n\n- Hands:\n  - Long fingers with slightly elongated joints  \n  - Slight webbing between digits\n  - Slightly colder to the touch\n\n- Face:\n  - Soft angular features\n  - Ethereal appearance\n  - Calm, distant expressions\n\n- Ears:\n  - Slightly elongated\n  - Finned edges common among older bloodlines\n\n- Markings:\n  - Natural glowing tide-like markings\n  - Resemble flowing currents and waves\n  - Intensify during spellcasting\n\n- Body:\n  - Lean and graceful build\n  - Fluid movements\n  - Naturally buoyant in water\n\n---",
              "racialCharacteristicsMarkdown": "| Characteristic | Buff/Debuff | Stat Rolls | Characteristics Tier Cap |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------ |\n| Strength       | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 3                   |\n| Dexterity      | +1          | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Agility        | +1          | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Constitution   | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Endurance      | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Intelligence   | -1          | 4d6        | Tier 3                   |\n| Wisdom         | +2          | 4d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Charisma       | -4          | 4d6        | Tier 1                   |\n| Luck           | 0           | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n\n---",
              "racialTraitsMarkdown": "### Amphibious Nature\nUniden can breathe both air and water, easily adapting between land and aquatic environments.\n\n### Waterborne Healing\nWhen immersed in a natural source of water (like rivers or rain), Undines are able to regenerate health quicker:\n- In combat: +3 HP per round  \n- Out of combat: +10 HP per round \n\n---\n### Drowned Soul\n#### Description\nThe sea carries countless memories of those it has claimed. Drownedborn Undien possess an innate connection to these lingering echoes.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Gain +2 on Spirit-related checks.\n- Can sense locations where death by drowning has occurred.\n- Gain advantage when interacting with water-bound spirits.\n\n---\n### Echoes of the Lost\n#### Description\nWater remembers. By touching natural bodies of water, a Drownedborn may perceive fragments of memories carried within the current.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Gain advantage when investigating shipwrecks, submerged ruins, and missing persons cases.\n- The GM may provide visions, emotions, sounds, or symbolic clues tied to events that occurred in nearby waters.\n- Receive a +2 bonus to Investigation checks involving aquatic mysteries.\n\n---\n\n### Call of the Depths\n\n#### Description\nThe ocean whispers warnings and secrets to its children.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Gain +2 Perception while within 30 metres of a natural body of water.\n- Detect hidden submerged objects within 9 metres.\n- Gain advantage when searching for underwater structures, shipwrecks, or hidden passages.\n\n---",
